<title>FINLAND: Finnish final March trade surplus FIM 3.5 bln-NCB.</title>
<headline>Finnish final March trade surplus FIM 3.5 bln-NCB.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's trade surplus rose to 3.47 billion markka in March from 3.19 billion in February and from 2.96 billion in March last year, the National Customs Board (NCB) said in statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The NCB earlier reported preliminary March trade surplus at 3.5 billion markka.</p>
<p>The value of exports rose six percent year-on-year in March and the value of imports rose three percent, the NCB said.</p>
<p>Trade balance (million markka): @</p>
<p>		   Mar '97    Feb '97    Mar '96</p>
<p> Exports	 16,043     14,839     15,114</p>
<p> Imports	 12,575     11,647     12,152</p>
<p> Balance	 +3,468     +3,192     +2,962</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
